sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Scheduler (BullMQ repeatable)
    participant P as OutboxDrainProcessor
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant Q as Queues/Handlers
    participant C as ProcessedEvent

    S->>P: outbox-drain tick (every OUTBOX_DRAIN_INTERVAL_MS, default 5000)
    P->>DB: Claim batch (status PENDING, nextAttemptAt <= now) FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED LIMIT 100
    loop For each claimed event
        P->>P: Build dispatch outside transaction
        P->>Q: Publish/dispatch by event type
        alt Success
            P->>DB: Mark event PUBLISHED (publishedAt)
        else Failure
            P->>DB: Increment attemptCount, set lastError, compute nextAttemptAt (backoff)
            alt attempts >= max
                P->>DB: Mark FAILED/DEAD per policy
            end
        end
    end
    Q->>C: Consumer inserts into ProcessedEvent (orgId, consumer, eventId)
    Note over C: Unique (organizationId, consumer, eventId) prevents double processing
    Note over P: Payloads contain IDs only, never PHI
    Note over P: Both API and worker run same AppModule; SCHEDULER_ENABLED gates scheduling
